)$ is given by\n\n$$\nm{y}^{″}=-ky+F(t).\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values for $m$ and $F(t)$ gives\n\n$$\n0.6{y}^{″}=-ky-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t).\n$$\n\nSimplifying and rearranging the above equation, we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{5k}{3}y=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t).\n$$\n\nThe complementary solution ${y}_{c}$ here represents simple harmonic motion, and it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants of integration, and $\\omega $ is the system's internal frequency.\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\n{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{5k}{3}\\,⟹\\,k=\\frac{3}{5}{\\omega }^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe oscillator experiences resonance when the frequency of the external periodic force $f(t)=-5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t),$ which is $5,$ is equal to the frequency of the complementary solution $\\omega .$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{3}{5}{\\omega }^{2}=\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot {5}^{2}=15\\,{\\text{kg/s}}^{2}.\n$$" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380807 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380808 13194139536046 true] [17592186380807 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536046 true] [17592186380807 1041 "field-1" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380807 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380808 13194139536046 true] [17592186380807 1110 #uuid "def07b86-c2d2-5c0b-97bc-3d4d516c1354" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380808 1034 "15" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380808 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536046 true] [17592186380808 1111 #uuid "c23c651d-0acd-57c4-8545-0d8e901058cb" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380809 1017 #edb/ref 17592186380810 13194139536046 true] [17592186380809 1089 "q-343679" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380809 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536046 true] [17592186380809 1100 "A particle of mass $0.8\\,\\text{kg}$ is attached to a massless spring. An external periodic force $F(t)=2cos\\,(\\frac{5}{2}t)\\,\\text{N}$ is applied to the particle.\n\nThe position of the particle is $y(t)$ (measured in meters), and $t>0$ is the time in se