r solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $D=\\frac{3}{2}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n- $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n- $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{1}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nOnly solutions I and II match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380828 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380829 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380830 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380831 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1000 #edb/ref 17592186380832 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1041 "selection" 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1104 #edb/ref 17592186380831 13194139536046 true] [17592186380827 1110 #uuid "66468e49-8da9-54cd-9ea2-0083e0b7f591" 13194